tion scientific report continuation preserves original and explicit hydrology review editions separately, then exports both saved reports with their editable study history and reads them with the independently restored application. Received Studies exposes exact saved Published-review source cards, native editor navigation, original selected-record/interpretation/review ZIP downloads and explicit report replace/append. The complete original source binding and filters are checked before direct editor navigation; current local draft/lifecycle takes precedence over delayed replies. The maintained installer composes the original received-study registration and declared assets without removing peer handlers. The outgoing exact product and every delivered attachment must be opened, visually inspected and used under the owner rule in operator/RECEIVED_PUBLISHED_REVIEWS.md; preserve the October13 14:00UTC cutoff. Captured external saved reviews can be explicitly admitted through the original importer and editor; original source bindings and admission provenance remain portable with later selected reviews. Carry CURRENT_OWNER_DIRECTION.md version 2026-10-13.3 and application AGENTS into the existing native course. The Three and Twenty Creek 2026 builtin retains the unchanged 57-file original source edition and all242 selected ResultIdentifiers, with explicit agreeing activity/characteristic weighting for142 measurements. Full raw-ID exports and grouped source provenance remain distinct. The maintained native receiving course continues this exact study through saved review and project restore. ECSA4100 recipient review rendering and current guarded shared-Study hooks remain exact. The original historical Three and Twenty study retains all73 source members and1502 original results; generated metadata binds its one source-owned statistical exclusion to original index/hash/row/ResultIdentifier. Native summaries use1501 eligible rows, while original chronology and source exports 